      '**Read 2 John 7–9.** Many deceivers have gone out into the world, those who do not confess that Jesus Christ came in the flesh. This is the deceiver and the antichrist. Watch yourselves, so that you do not lose the things you have worked for. “Whoever transgresses and doesn’t remain in the teaching of Christ, doesn’t have God. He who remains in the teaching has both the Father and the Son.”\n\nThe teaching to remain in is the teaching of Christ, and this letter names the part being denied: he came in the flesh. Going beyond that teaching is not progress. John says the one who does so does not have God. This is the rule for every note in this Bible. Stay in what Christ and his apostles taught. Do not add.\n\nReceive into the house the teachers who remain in that doctrine. Do not greet the others as fellow workers (verses 10–11).',
