      '**Read 3 John 1–4.** The elder loves Gaius in truth. He rejoices greatly when brothers come and testify to the truth that is in Gaius, even as he walks in truth. “I have no greater joy than this: to hear about my children walking in truth.”\n\nTruth is not only a list to defend. It is a walk. The love John names is “in truth.” Later he commends support for strangers who went out for the sake of the Name, taking nothing from the Gentiles (verses 5–8). Walking in truth sends practical help to true workers.\n\nDo not separate a warm heart from the truth. John’s joy is children who walk in it.',
