    title: 'The Faith Once for All Delivered',
    summary: 'Jude urges you to contend for the faith once for all delivered to the saints. Certain people have crept in who deny our only Master and Lord, Jesus Christ.',
    bodyMd:
      '**Read Jude 3–4.** Jude was eager to write about our common salvation, and he found it necessary to write urging you to contend earnestly for the faith which was once for all delivered to the saints. Certain men have crept in, long ago written about for this condemnation, ungodly men, turning the grace of our God into indecency, and denying our only Master and Lord, Jesus Christ.\n\n“Once for all” means the faith was delivered. It is not waiting for a later edition. Contending is required because grace is being twisted into a license to sin, and the Master is being denied. Jude will remind them of judgments God has already spoken — Israel in the wilderness, the angels, Sodom — and he will point them to the Lord coming with his holy ones. Contend for what was delivered. Do not add to it, and do not let it be turned into indecency.\n\nMercy, peace, and love are multiplied to those who are called, beloved in God the Father, and kept for Jesus Christ (verses 1–2). Contend as one who is kept.',
