    bodyMd:
      '**Read Revelation 5:1–10.** A scroll, sealed with seven seals, is in the right hand of him who sits on the throne. No one in heaven or on earth or under the earth is worthy to open it. John weeps. An elder says, “Don’t weep. Behold, the Lion who is of the tribe of Judah, the Root of David, has overcome so that he can open the book.” John looks and sees a Lamb standing, as though it had been slain, with seven horns and seven eyes. The living creatures and the elders fall down and sing a new song: “You are worthy to take the book and to open its seals, for you were killed, and bought us for God with your blood out of every tribe, language, people, and nation, and made us kings and priests to our God.”\n\nThe Lion is the Lamb. The Root of David is the slain one. Worthiness is not raw power. It is the blood that purchased a people. That is Exodus 12 and Isaiah 53 and Psalm 110’s priest, gathered in one vision. The people are from every tribe, which is the promise to Abraham reaching the nations (Genesis 12:3; Revelation 5:9).\n\nWorship the Lamb who was slain. Do not weep as if no one were worthy. Someone is.',
