    bodyMd:
      '**Read Revelation 21:1–8.** A new heaven and a new earth, for the first heaven and the first earth have passed away, and the sea is no more. The holy city, New Jerusalem, comes down out of heaven from God, prepared as a bride adorned for her husband. A loud voice: “Behold, God’s dwelling is with people, and he will dwell with them, and they will be his people, and God himself will be with them as their God.” He will wipe away every tear. Death will be no more, nor mourning, nor crying, nor pain. The first things have passed away. He who sits on the throne says, “Behold, I am making all things new.” These words are faithful and true. “I will give to him who is thirsty from the spring of the water of life freely. He who overcomes, I will give him these things. I will be his God, and he will be my son.”\n\nThis is Genesis remade, and it is the covenant sentence of Jeremiah and Leviticus: “I will be their God, and they will be my people.” It comes after the Lamb’s wedding, not instead of the cross. Verse 8 still names those who have their part in the lake of fire, including the unbelieving. The promise and the warning are both written.\n\nThirst, and take the water freely. Overcome by belonging to the Lamb, not by pretending the warning is missing.',
